f8739b.png)\n\nIn $△OPR$ shown above, we have \n\n- $OP=4|p|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OP}$ and $p$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OP}=4p.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $PR=2|q|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ has the opposite direction to $q$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PR}=-2q.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PR} \\\\  & =4p-2q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $r=\\lambda p+\\mu q=4p-2q.$\n\nSince $p∦q,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =4$ and $\\mu =-2$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd56d06731bf3a892817106cbdb95ceb9c384088c6beda0f637b80eae6fe7989"} {"question" "q-120277" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "11c191ae8e2641d8e32dc83a684af92f102dca348edd2c027c4163fe1ba2fdfb"} {"question" "q-120277" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd56d06731bf3a892817106cbdb95ceb9c384088c6beda0f637b80eae6fe7989"} {"question" "q-120277" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =4$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\mu =-4$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\mu =2$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =4$ and $\\mu =-2$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =4$ and $\\mu =-4$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd56d06731bf3a892817106cbdb95ceb9c384088c6beda0f637b80eae6fe7989"} {"question" "q-120277" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$\\lambda =4$ and $\\mu =-2$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd56d06731bf3a892817106cbdb95ceb9c384088c6beda0f637b80eae6fe7989"} {"question" "q-120285" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/assets/c4d26b3db6446f586ca47634d9f9a3a004968a0081b8859ce46b4b4af799d066.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OH}=h,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OI}=i$ and $J$ divides $\\overset{―}{HI}$ in the ratio $HJ:JI=3:7.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OJ}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd56d06731bf3a892817106cbdb95ceb9c384088c6beda0f637b80eae6fe7989"} {"question" "q-120285" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\overset{\\to }{OH}+\\overset{\\to }{HJ}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OH}=h,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{HJ}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OHI,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{HI} & =\\overset{\\to }{HO}+\\overset{\\to }{OI} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OH}+\\overset{\\to }{OI} \\\\  & =-h+i \\\\  & =i-h.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $HJ:JI=3:7,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{HJ}=\\frac{3}{10}\\overset{\\to }{HI}=\\frac{3}{10}(i-h).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OJ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OH}+\\overset{\\to }{HJ} \\\\  & =h+\\frac{3}{10}(i-h) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{10}h+\\frac{3}{10}i.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd56d06731bf3a892817106cbdb95ceb9c384088c6beda0f637b80eae6fe7989"} {"question" "q-120285" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "11c191ae8e2641d8e32dc83a684af92f102dca348edd2c027c4163fe1ba2fdfb"} {"question" "q-120285" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd56d06731bf3a892817106cbdb95ceb9c384088c6beda0f637b80eae6fe7989"} {"question" "q-120285" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{1}{2}h+\\frac{1}{2}i"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{2}{5}h+\\frac{3}{5}i"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{3}{10}h+\\frac{7}{10}i"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{3}{5}h+\\frac{2}{5}i"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{7}{10}h+\\frac{3}{10}i"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd56d06731bf3a892817106cbdb95ceb9c384088c6beda0f637b80eae6fe7989"} {"question" "q-120285" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{7}{10}h+\\frac{3}{10}i"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd56d06731bf3a892817106cbdb95ceb9c384088c6beda0f637b80eae6fe7989"} {"question" "q-325974" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/assets/bae20e625c529ef2157faa4d534a19529c605c9002ed750e56723ff29e265226.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $c=\\lambda a-4b,$ then\n\n$\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd56d06731bf3a892817106cbdb95ceb9c384088c6beda0f637b80eae6fe7989"} {"question" "q-325974" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=\\lambda a-4b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $-4b.$ So, we first draw the vector $-4b$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/assets/139a4d4312ecbe42cd3a3859af4f4d7b93f8bbc54548ac5a0244c04e7ba5287b.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $-4b.$ Then\n\n$$\nc=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=3|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $a$ have opposite directions\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=-3a.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =-4b-3a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a-4b=-3a-4b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd56d06731bf3a892817106cbdb95ceb9c384088c6beda0f637b80eae6fe7989"} {"question" "q-325974" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "11c191ae8e2641d8e32dc83a684af92f102dca348edd2c027c4163fe1ba2fdfb"} {"question" "q-325974" "field" "field-1