ac{1}{2}k.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\nt=\\overset{\\to }{OX}+\\overset{\\to }{XT}=-2j-\\frac{1}{2}k.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $t=\\lambda j+\\mu k=-2j-\\frac{1}{2}k.$\n\nSince $k∦j,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =-\\frac{1}{2}$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186244958 17592186244960 17592186245021 17592186245022 17592186245023 17592186245024 17592186245025] "immutable_fields" [[17592186244957 :answer-field/correct] [17592186244957 :answer-field/id] [17592186244957 :answer-field/key] [17592186244957 :answer-field/type] [17592186244959 :answer-field/correct] [17592186244959 :answer-field/id] [17592186244959 :answer-field/key] [17592186244959 :answer-field/type] [17592186245020 :answer-field/correct] [17592186245020 :answer-field/id] [17592186245020 :answer-field/key] [17592186245020 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
